  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e2f7b0-6e0e-4a2b-9a1a-skoutcrm00001",
    "name": "Skout CRM (@skout/crm)",
    "description": "Native Revenue Workspace API — companies, contacts, deals, pipelines/stages, tasks, activities, meetings, and a dashboard overview.\n\nAuth: local/dev uses stub auth via the `x-stub-user-email` header (set in the collection variable `stubEmail`). All requests in a workspace share the same `x-stub-user-email` → same workspace. Change `stubEmail` to simulate a different workspace/user.\n\nRun order for the golden path: Health → Companies → Contacts → Pipelines → Deals → Deal stage change → Activities → Tasks → Meetings → Dashboard. IDs are captured automatically into collection variables by each request's test script, so requests later in the collection can reuse them.\n\nDestructive actions (DELETE) require the `owner` role — the first stub user in a workspace is always `owner`; there's no invite/join flow yet, so testing the `member`-role 403 path requires directly inserting a `workspace_members` row (see the e2e test `role-based permissions` cases for the pattern).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3002", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "stubEmail", "value": "crm-postman@test.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "companyId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "contactId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
